cff-version: 1.2.0
title: contract-assay
message: >-
  If you use this benchmark, or report a figure measured with it, please cite it
  and say which corpus commit you measured against. A figure without the corpus
  commit is not reproducible: the records, their locators and the pinned sources
  all move between releases.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Boik
    family-names: Su
    email: boik.su@cycraft.com
    affiliation: CyCraft Technology
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4700-7128
repository-code: https://github.com/qazbnm456/contract-assay
license: MIT
version: 0.1.2
abstract: >-
  Benchmark infrastructure for LLM smart contract auditing. A prediction is
  scored only if it quotes the source at the lines it names, and the quote is
  checked against a pinned commit before scoring, so a detector that names a
  plausible line without reading the file measures nothing. Ships a corpus of
  478 verified records across nine vulnerability classes, drawn from public
  audit platforms, with the adjudication for each record recorded next to it.
keywords:
  - smart-contract
  - security
  - benchmark
  - llm
  - solidity
  - audit
  - vulnerability-detection
